Entity Catalog

A global, category-agnostic Entity Catalog that stores basic metadata about any organization in any country.

Features

Minimal PostgreSQL core for entity storage

Optional metadata catalog for raw packages

Semi-structured text suggestions, discovery worker, and manual admin import

Stateless microservices:

Matching layer (fuzzy + phonetic)

Scraper adapter with robots.txt respect

Region resolver with caching

Cache aggregator

Full authentication + role-based access control

Prometheus metrics

Admin audit logging + merge dry-run

Production-ready Dockerfile + healthcheck

Repository Structure
/migrations/...
/src/services/...
/src/controllers/...
/src/routes/...
/workers/...
/docs/ENTITY_CATALOG.md
/tests/...
Dockerfile.prod

Getting Started
1. Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/<YOUR_USERNAME>/entity-catalog.git
cd entity-catalog

2. Install Dependencies
npm install

3. Environment

Create a .env file using .env.example:

cp .env.example .env


Fill in your database, Redis, and auth credentials.

4. Database Migrations
npx sequelize db:migrate


Verify migrations:

npm test tests/migration.test.js

5. Running Tests
npm test


All unit tests for workers, services, endpoints, metrics, and region caching are included.

6. Start Application
npm run dev

7. API Endpoints

Entity

GET    /api/v1/entity?country=XX&region=YY&category=any
GET    /api/v1/entity/:id
POST   /api/v1/entity/import/manual
POST   /api/v1/entity/suggest
POST   /api/v1/entity/:id/refresh-metadata


Rules

All write operations require authentication

RBAC applied: system, admin, reader

Metrics

GET /metrics

8. Workers

entityDiscovery.worker.js → Scrapes public directories, inserts/updates entities

metadataIngestion.worker.js → Stores raw JSON from structured sources

9. Docker (Production)
docker build -f Dockerfile.prod -t entity-catalog .
docker run -d -p 3000:3000 --env-file .env entity-catalog
curl http://localhost:3000/healthz

10. Metrics

Prometheus metrics exposed at /metrics:

entity_created_total

entity_updated_total

metadata_packages_imported_total

discovery_run_duration_seconds

scrape_error_total

cache_hit_ratio

11. Admin Audit Logging

All admin actions (merge, edit, toggle) logged in admin_audit_log table. Dry-run mode supported.

12. Security & Compliance

No secrets in repo

.env excluded in .gitignore

Scraper respects robots.txt

Rate-limited requests with retry/backoff